# A completed added kan (kakan) cancels an opponent's ippatsu
# (engine.md §4.2 Ippatsu, rules.md §4.26).
# Turn 1: Seat 0 discards 5z -> Seat 1 calls pon:55z, discards 9s. Seats 2, 3 tsumogiri.
# Turn 2: Seat 0 declares riichi (holding one 2p dora from ind 1p -> riichi+pinfu+tanyao+dora:1 = 4 han 30 fu).
# Seat 1 draws 4th 5z, declares kakan 5z (no robber -> kakan completes, cancelling Seat 0's ippatsu!),
# draws rinshan 7s, and discards 7s -> Seat 0 rons 7s WITHOUT ippatsu!
# Scoring for Seat 0 (dealer, East):
#   Hand: 234m 678m 234p 56s 88p + ron 7s (dora ind 1p -> dora 2p, +1; kan dora ind 1z adds 0; ura ind 7z, 6z add 0)
#   Yaku: riichi (1) + pinfu (1) + tanyao (1) + dora:1 (2p) = 4 han 30 fu (NO ippatsu!)
#   Dealer 4 han 30 fu ron = 11600 from Seat 1 (with ippatsu it would be 12000).

